{"name":"Treasure Casket","hex":"#9b7856","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"treasure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collection of valuable things; accumulated wealth; a stock of money, jewels, etc.","Anything greatly valued.\n\nA term of endearment.\n\n The female genitals; pudenda."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider to be precious; to value highly.","To store or stow in a safe place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure"},{"term":"casket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A little box, e.g. for jewellery.","An urn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put into, or preserve in, a casket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure","wikidata":"Q272937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/1280px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Howard Pyle's illustration of pirates burying Captain Kidd's treasure, from Howard Pyle's Book of Pirate